From c7464757dea446cac20d4a9732a90f179104fd6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:33:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1023/1198] Import a track from elsewhere: it becomes a take
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HERESY 1023. Post has "Import a track": a WAV, FLAC, MP3 (M4A, OGG, AIFF) from
anywhere — a SUNO track — goes up with a progress line and becomes an ordinary
take in the library, converted to 48 kHz 24-bit WAV, the original kept beside
it, marked imported; optional lyrics go with it for the lyrics check. Then it
opens in Post, where stems, remaster, spectrum and lyrics check work on it as
on the Kit's own takes.
The Kit server passes POST /lab/… to heresy-lab (bodies up to 1 GB, a 120 s
read timeout for slow uploads).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
